    "why_matters": "The bulletin gives a public, weekly EU reference price for LPG motor fuel before taxes, the kind of published price the fuel cost of an LPG van or site vehicle fleet, or a rate indexed to it can be set against; the bulletin states no surcharge rule, so how fast a move reaches an invoice depends on each counterparty's terms. Each country's duties and VAT come on top of this pre-tax figure. The price trajectory on this page puts the latest held week above both earlier held weeks, with no one-week change held for it. Directive (EU) 2023/959, held on this site as a regulation brief, brings fuels released for consumption for buildings and road transport into a second emissions trading system, whose suppliers report the share of the allowance cost passed on to consumers.",
